Subject: Gives the register backend its own dense per-function PIC site numbering

What this does
  Gives the register backend its own dense per-function PIC site numbering.

Why we need it
  Register property instructions carried the shared stack inline-cache slot index, so there was no register-owned place to put a cache.

What it adds
  Adds `JSFunctionBytecode.regvm_pic`/`regvm_pic_count`, a `pic` base on `JSRegRun` set at record fill, entry and threaded rebind, dense site assignment for `get_field`/`get_field2`/`get_arg_field`/`put_field`/`put_field_xfer`/`get_local_field`/`get_length`, site validation against the new count, and `regvm_pic_count` in the register program header; `ROP_get_length` gains a site operand.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. Regenerated register blobs are in 9999. `BC_VERSION` is unchanged.
